"public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 14, "impression_count": 12632, "like_count": 219, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 5, "retweet_count": 11}, "text": "Hearing reports that a noted DC-area food blogger tried to use an LLM to criticize empirical tax research, and it did not go well", "url": "https://x.com/M_C_Klein/status/2115851061273715089"}, {"author_id": "733647469305864195", "created_at": "2026-10-29T16:37:58.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115845608796021094"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/d2p1IPiZvn", "end": 268, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Brad_Setser/status/2115845608796021094/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115845521722232835", "start": 245, "url": "https://t.co/d2p1IPiZvn"}]}, "id": "2115845608796021094", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 12, "impression_count": 6028, "like_count": 20, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 7, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "A couple of random observations about the US GDP data --\n\none is that service consumption growth seems to have increased relative to goods consumption growth in the post pandemic years (helps with GDP, less imported content in services).  \n\n1/2 https://t.co/d2p1IPiZvn", "url": "https://x.com/Brad_Setser/status/2115845608796021094"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-10-29T16:28:39.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115843263265685559"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/econberger/sta…", "end": 191, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/econberger/status/2115833176220475447", "start": 168, "url": "https://t.co/rdwWXiag6X"}]}, "id": "2115843263265685559", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1283, "like_count": 13, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115833176220475447", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "It speaks highly of economist academia that a lot of experts who are critical of the research being slop-audited were nevertheless even more critical of the slop-audit https://t.co/rdwWXiag6X", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2115843263265685559"}, {"author_id": "733647469305864195", "created_at": "2026-10-29T16:03:57.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115837047386886496"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/jasonfurman/st…", "end": 295, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/jasonfurman/status/2115814704241344965", "start": 272, "url": "https://t.co/iCkx2JHBc4"}]}, "id": "2115837047386886496", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4035, "like_count": 6, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115814704241344965", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "And q1 25 was tariff front running (pharma especially)\n\nTho to be fair to q3 6, the large swing in net exports was in part a normalization after of some of the after effects of front running faded.  But it was mostly a real surge in capital goods imports for data centers https://t.co/iCkx2JHBc4", "url": "https://x.com/Brad_Setser/status/2115837047386886496"}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "14096763", "name": "Joe Weisenthal", "username": "TheStalwart"}, {"id": "702235316812275712", "name": "Guy Berger", "username": "EconBerger"}, {"id": "2220183580", "name": "George Magnus", "username": "georgemagnus1"}, {"id": "497231011", "name": "China Beige Book", "username": "ChinaBeigeBook"}, {"id": "2961589380", "name": "Liz Ann Sonders", "username": "LizAnnSonders"}, {"id": "3039504459", "name": "Physical Review Letters", "username": "PhysRevLett"}, {"id": "961132338", "name": "Matthew C. Klein", "username": "M_C_Klein"}, {"id": "733647469305864195", "name": "Brad Setser", "username": "Brad_Setser"}]}, "meta": {"newest_id": "2115901144451219833", "next_token": "b26v89c19zqg8o3juzlxoawlj5a8axtwqgyka4fu9k7st", "oldest_id": "2115837047386886496", "result_count": 25}}
